# No pass-through functions

Do not add a function, method, or arrow whose body only returns another call with the same arguments. Call that function at the use site.

A rename, a Vue template helper, or a "clearer name" is not a reason to keep the wrapper.

```ts
// Bad — rowLocales exists only to call findingLocales
function rowLocales(finding: ReportFinding) {
  return findingLocales(finding)
}

// Good
findingLocales(finding)
```

Keep a wrapper when its body does something else: maps or drops arguments, filters the result, catches errors, or satisfies an interface that must delegate.
